(text "XTAL - 25 MHz  |  ECS ECX-2236  |  ECS-250-8-36CKM-TR  |  Pierce oscillator" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 14.00 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7fbb6367-96bc-4e01-8e7c-a563b7edbf52"))
(text "House-common passives: load caps 12 pF C0G 0603, Rext 0R jumper, Rf 1M (DNP). Typical use: Ethernet PHYs / switches." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 19.30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b513792f-595e-4e68-a518-5385fbe80339"))
(text "DESIGN EQUATIONS - 25 MHz crystal, ECS-250-8-36CKM-TR (ECS ECX-2236); refs: ST AN2867 / TI SZZA043 / TI SLAA322\nCrystal: CL = 8 pF, ESR max = 60 ohm\n  C0 max = 5 pF, drive level max = 100 uW (datasheet), fundamental mode. Uses: Ethernet PHYs / switches\nLoad caps: C1 = C2 = 2*(CL - Cs), Cs = 2.0 pF (pin + trace, edit for your layout) = 12.0 pF -> 12 pF C0G 5% (house value)\n  Effective CL = C1*C2/(C1+C2) + Cs = 6 + 2.0 = 8.0 pF (+0.0 pF vs spec)\nPulling: S = C1m/(2*(C0+CL)^2) ~ 8.9 ppm/pF (C1m ~3 fF typ, assumed) ; 5% cap tol -> dCL +/-0.30 pF -> +/-2.7 ppm\nOscillation margin: gm_crit = 4*ESR*(2*pi*f)^2*(C0+CL)^2 = 1.001 mA/V\n  Gain margin = gm(osc)/gm_crit >= 5 -> oscillator gm must exceed 5.00 mA/V (check MCU datasheet HSE/LSE gm)\nDrive level @ 1.0 Vpp on XOUT: DL = ESR*(2*pi*f*(C0+CL)*Vpp/(2*sqrt2))^2 = 31.27 uW vs 100 uW max -> OK\nDrive level @ 3.3 Vpp on XOUT: DL = ESR*(2*pi*f*(C0+CL)*Vpp/(2*sqrt2))^2 = 340.58 uW vs 100 uW max -> EXCEEDED - fit Rext\nRext (series, XOUT side): start value 1/(2*pi*f*C2) = 0.53 kohm ; fitted 0R (house jumper) - populate only if DL exceeded,\n  then re-check gain margin with ESR -> ESR + Rext. Rf 1M (house) shown DNP: fit only if the oscillator has no internal feedback resistor.\nLayout: C1/C2 and crystal within ~5 mm of the pins, GND guard ring, no signals under the crystal, return C1/C2 to the oscillator GND pin." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 128.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left top)) (uuid "61c922e1-35ec-4264-8c44-9397b6a3c643"))
